1
00:00:04,065 --> 00:00:04,905
Let's break up.

2
00:00:04,985 --> 00:00:06,945
I can't date someone
who's in love with my best friend.

3
00:00:07,025 --> 00:00:08,825
We know about you and Lee.

4
00:00:08,905 --> 00:00:11,145
I could've let it go that you lied to me.

5
00:00:11,225 --> 00:00:12,545
But I can't.

6
00:00:12,625 --> 00:00:13,585
I'm quitting this club.

7
00:00:13,665 --> 00:00:15,465
I never wanted to be
in this damn club anyway.

8
00:00:15,545 --> 00:00:16,545
"DON'T" DATE SOMEONE CLOSE TO YOU!

9
00:00:16,625 --> 00:00:18,065
Welcome, everyone,

10
00:00:18,145 --> 00:00:21,305
to Next Gen E-sports Thailand.

11
00:00:21,385 --> 00:00:22,625
Hey!

12
00:00:22,705 --> 00:00:24,745
Putter, you can do this! I believe in you!

13
00:00:24,825 --> 00:00:28,025
And the winner of this qualifier is Team…

14
00:00:28,105 --> 00:00:30,385
Fire Storm!

15
00:00:30,465 --> 00:00:32,345
Let's just go back to being friends.

16
00:00:32,425 --> 00:00:36,065
I think it'd be better for us
and everyone else, don't you?

17
00:00:37,585 --> 00:00:38,745
Love and friendship.

18
00:00:38,825 --> 00:00:41,185
are equally hard to walk away from.

19
00:00:41,265 --> 00:00:44,705
Especially when you two
already broke up, but he's still around.

20
00:00:44,785 --> 00:00:46,305
Then it's even harder.

21
00:00:46,385 --> 00:00:48,905
So, you encouraged them
to talk things out?

22
00:00:48,985 --> 00:00:49,945
Yeah.

23
00:00:50,025 --> 00:00:52,305
Otherwise, it would just stay unclear.

24
00:00:52,385 --> 00:00:53,905
That would be hard on everyone.

25
00:00:53,985 --> 00:00:55,905
If you change your mind, let me know.

26
00:00:55,985 --> 00:00:57,825
I think he wants you there.

27
00:00:57,905 --> 00:00:59,025
Yeah.

28
00:00:59,105 --> 00:01:01,025
I told him.

29
00:01:01,105 --> 00:01:04,825
Friendship is precious,
and it lasts the longest.

30
00:01:04,905 --> 00:01:07,665
But… it's hard to say something like that.

31
00:01:07,745 --> 00:01:12,105
It might sound funny,
but that day, I practiced.

32
00:01:12,185 --> 00:01:13,985
I rehearsed my speech before seeing him.

33
00:01:15,265 --> 00:01:18,825
All this… is just to tell you…

34
00:01:20,665 --> 00:01:21,865
I like you.

35
00:01:22,465 --> 00:01:24,585
Break the rule… and be my boyfriend.

36
00:01:25,345 --> 00:01:26,385
Shit.

37
00:01:27,425 --> 00:01:28,785
What the hell am I saying?

38
00:01:41,145 --> 00:01:42,105
Putter.

39
00:01:43,345 --> 00:01:46,105
I believe you, that you don't like Indy.

40
00:01:48,305 --> 00:01:49,705
But right now,

41
00:01:50,545 --> 00:01:54,065
I'm afraid… I'll end up
feeling this way again.

42
00:01:56,865 --> 00:02:01,065
We might get back together
just to break up again.

43
00:02:01,745 --> 00:02:03,465
And I don't want to lose you.

44
00:02:05,105 --> 00:02:07,985
It's just… I think…

45
00:02:08,065 --> 00:02:09,105
Let's go back to being friends.

46
00:02:16,345 --> 00:02:18,785
It'd be better for us… and everyone else.

47
00:02:19,585 --> 00:02:20,545
Don't you think?

48
00:02:23,465 --> 00:02:24,825
I practiced this.

49
00:02:25,625 --> 00:02:28,185
But when I saw you,
I still couldn't say it all.

50
00:02:34,665 --> 00:02:37,025
Yeah. I agree.

51
00:02:38,785 --> 00:02:40,705
We'll get to mess with each other again.

52
00:02:41,785 --> 00:02:44,665
Staying like this
has been so damn awkward.

53
00:02:45,545 --> 00:02:47,105
I'm tired of acting.

54
00:02:51,185 --> 00:02:54,545
So… friends again, okay?

55
00:03:01,025 --> 00:03:04,625
Yeah, of course.
Want me to smack you to prove it?

56
00:03:04,705 --> 00:03:06,145
Hey, no, thanks.

57
00:03:06,225 --> 00:03:08,465
Do something friends would do.
Don't be ridiculous.

58
00:03:12,145 --> 00:03:13,145
Fine.

59
00:03:13,785 --> 00:03:15,225
Then I'll roast you myself.

60
00:03:16,865 --> 00:03:19,305
Roast me at the restaurant. I'm starving.

61
00:03:31,585 --> 00:03:34,225
Do you think… they'll get back together?

62
00:03:35,185 --> 00:03:37,705
-I think they'll get back together.
-I don't think so.

63
00:03:39,305 --> 00:03:41,665
Yeah. Which way's the restaurant?

64
00:03:43,145 --> 00:03:44,505
That way.

65
00:03:44,585 --> 00:03:45,505
Let's go.

66
00:03:47,465 --> 00:03:50,785
You don't have to carry it. I'll carry it.

67
00:03:52,065 --> 00:03:54,665
Your loss. Less work for me.

68
00:03:59,065 --> 00:04:00,305
They're here.
Let's pretend we don't see them.

69
00:04:00,385 --> 00:04:01,665
They're here.

70
00:04:01,745 --> 00:04:03,625
-They're here.
-They're here.

71
00:04:03,705 --> 00:04:04,545
Come on.

72
00:04:04,625 --> 00:04:07,025
-Go, go, go.
-Hurry, hurry.

73
00:04:07,105 --> 00:04:08,065
You go.

74
00:04:08,145 --> 00:04:09,545
-Go already.
-Go on.

75
00:04:09,625 --> 00:04:11,065
You go too.

76
00:05:40,305 --> 00:05:42,465
My stomach's about to burst.

77
00:05:45,385 --> 00:05:46,625
Whoa.

78
00:05:46,705 --> 00:05:49,905
With the lights on,
the room feels so much brighter.

79
00:05:50,705 --> 00:05:52,025
Yeah, totally.

80
00:05:52,105 --> 00:05:54,425
Last week, I thought
you were saving electricity.

81
00:05:56,945 --> 00:05:58,505
I was just going for a dark vibe.

82
00:05:59,065 --> 00:06:02,665
Update your patch.
Nobody's that dark anymore.

83
00:06:04,505 --> 00:06:07,025
-Don't kill the mood.
-What?

84
00:06:09,185 --> 00:06:11,425
Nothing. Nothing.

85
00:06:13,545 --> 00:06:16,105
Got a little reward for you.
In the fridge.

86
00:06:16,705 --> 00:06:18,625
To celebrate you, Putter… and Fire Storm.

87
00:06:18,705 --> 00:06:19,585
Go check it out.

88
00:06:19,665 --> 00:06:21,345
-Yeah, I'm going.
-Go on, hurry.

89
00:06:28,025 --> 00:06:30,385
You bought five boxes? This many?

90
00:06:30,465 --> 00:06:32,705
I'm gonna get so fat. Let's share them.

91
00:06:32,785 --> 00:06:35,945
I bought that many…
just to hear you say that.

92
00:06:37,625 --> 00:06:38,905
Always scheming,
then calling it friendship.

93
00:06:39,505 --> 00:06:41,905
But… Thanks anyway.

94
00:06:51,025 --> 00:06:52,265
I got it from here.

95
00:07:08,065 --> 00:07:09,625
You gonna take a shower?

96
00:07:09,705 --> 00:07:11,025
If not, mind if I go first?

97
00:07:11,105 --> 00:07:12,425
Yeah.

98
00:07:12,505 --> 00:07:15,505
I'm glad… we're talking again.

99
00:07:16,505 --> 00:07:18,545
Yeah. Me too.

100
00:07:19,225 --> 00:07:22,385
And… don't forget
to clear things up with Indy.

101
00:07:22,465 --> 00:07:23,585
-Yeah.
-You're the only one left.

102
00:07:23,665 --> 00:07:24,785
Okay.

103
00:07:26,905 --> 00:07:27,985
See you tomorrow, Buddy.

104
00:07:29,625 --> 00:07:31,745
See you. Buddy.

105
00:08:33,305 --> 00:08:35,144
Shit. Sorry, traffic was awful.

106
00:09:08,225 --> 00:09:09,465
Nobody else is here yet?

107
00:09:17,305 --> 00:09:18,625
Guess they're running late.

108
00:09:22,585 --> 00:09:24,225
Didn't think you'd come.

109
00:09:26,905 --> 00:09:29,145
I… came to make things right.

110
00:09:34,545 --> 00:09:37,585
I'll go grab some drinks,
if nobody's here yet.

111
00:09:40,505 --> 00:09:41,385
Wait.

112
00:09:44,345 --> 00:09:45,465
I'll come with you.

113
00:09:46,585 --> 00:09:47,705
What do you want? I'll get it.

114
00:09:51,505 --> 00:09:52,585
It's just…

115
00:09:54,105 --> 00:09:56,105
I've got something to talk to you about.

116
00:09:58,465 --> 00:10:01,465
Come on. Been waiting for you to start.

117
00:10:01,545 --> 00:10:04,185
If you say some stupid shit again,
I'm punching you.

118
00:10:08,985 --> 00:10:10,545
Want a free punch first?

119
00:10:10,625 --> 00:10:12,065
I'm not a violent person.

120
00:10:13,545 --> 00:10:14,465
You're full of shit.

121
00:10:20,185 --> 00:10:22,465
I… I'm sorry.

122
00:10:23,225 --> 00:10:26,105
For… being such an idiot.

123
00:10:26,825 --> 00:10:28,345
None of it was your fault.

124
00:10:30,465 --> 00:10:33,185
Yeah. You were way out of line.

125
00:10:33,265 --> 00:10:35,425
Yeah. I'll take the blame for everything.

126
00:10:37,425 --> 00:10:38,785
I'll…

127
00:10:40,065 --> 00:10:41,145
buy you ten meals.

128
00:10:42,665 --> 00:10:44,385
That's all you've got to say?

129
00:10:47,585 --> 00:10:48,625
Here.

130
00:10:49,905 --> 00:10:52,585
We've already had our deep talk.
Have a seat.

131
00:11:00,865 --> 00:11:03,865
Didn't think I'd say this today,
but I'll say it.

132
00:11:07,065 --> 00:11:11,025
You… are the closest friend I've ever had.

133
00:11:13,625 --> 00:11:17,945
I… don't want anything…
to change what we have.

134
00:11:20,865 --> 00:11:22,345
The reason I got mad…

135
00:11:24,585 --> 00:11:26,105
was because I felt…

136
00:11:27,865 --> 00:11:28,905
like your replacement.

137
00:11:30,385 --> 00:11:33,625
I couldn't bring myself to be mad
at Putter, so I took it out on you.

138
00:11:34,265 --> 00:11:36,665
Which… I don't even know why.

139
00:11:40,705 --> 00:11:43,665
But no matter what,
I shouldn't have done that.

140
00:11:44,665 --> 00:11:46,305
I shouldn't have lied to you.

141
00:11:47,305 --> 00:11:48,465
Because you…

142
00:11:53,225 --> 00:11:55,225
care about me more than anyone.

143
00:11:57,745 --> 00:11:59,025
And I…

144
00:12:00,905 --> 00:12:02,145
care about you the most too.

145
00:12:28,385 --> 00:12:33,545
Honestly, I never thought…
we'd ever fight over love.

146
00:12:34,825 --> 00:12:35,665
Pretty cool.

147
00:12:47,345 --> 00:12:48,745
Oh, shit.

148
00:12:48,825 --> 00:12:50,465
I'm keeping this to blackmail you.

149
00:12:50,545 --> 00:12:53,625
If you ever act like an asshole again,
I'm posting every single one, dumbass.

150
00:12:53,705 --> 00:12:55,705
-So you were acting?
-Nope.

151
00:12:55,785 --> 00:12:57,945
I really was mad, just not that mad.

152
00:13:02,625 --> 00:13:04,225
Just don't do it again.

153
00:13:04,305 --> 00:13:05,665
That shitty attitude.

154
00:13:07,745 --> 00:13:08,945
Yes, Dad.

155
00:13:11,225 --> 00:13:12,105
This is something new, though.

156
00:13:12,865 --> 00:13:16,425
All the time we've been friends,
we've never thrown a punch.

157
00:13:17,305 --> 00:13:19,745
Never had a real fight.

158
00:13:19,825 --> 00:13:22,505
I actually want to complete
the best-friend checklist.

159
00:13:25,625 --> 00:13:27,705
I'll give you one. Want it?

160
00:13:27,785 --> 00:13:29,105
-Hell yeah, asshole.
-Hey, wait.

161
00:13:29,185 --> 00:13:30,905
-What's with you?
-Let me punch you first.

162
00:13:44,265 --> 00:13:46,265
-Surprise!
-Surprise!

163
00:13:48,585 --> 00:13:49,985
I knew it.

164
00:13:50,065 --> 00:13:52,265
If all of you were late,
it would be the end of the world.

165
00:13:52,345 --> 00:13:53,465
Yeah, whatever.

166
00:13:53,545 --> 00:13:55,545
Come on, let's take a picture.

167
00:13:55,625 --> 00:13:57,705
-I'm sending it to our group.
-Go, go.

168
00:13:57,785 --> 00:13:58,865
Go, go!

169
00:13:58,945 --> 00:14:00,665
-Put your arms around each other.
-Closer.

170
00:14:00,745 --> 00:14:01,665
That's it!

171
00:14:03,305 --> 00:14:04,145
Click.

172
00:14:49,225 --> 00:14:50,345
Putter.

173
00:14:52,105 --> 00:14:53,025
I'm sorry.

174
00:14:53,105 --> 00:14:55,065
That's enough. You're embarrassing me.

175
00:14:55,145 --> 00:14:56,465
I said wait for the right moment.

176
00:14:56,545 --> 00:14:58,545
Well, this is it.
Otherwise, I'll lose my nerve.

177
00:14:58,625 --> 00:15:01,465
-I'm sorry. I'm really sorry, Putter.
-That's enough!

178
00:15:04,105 --> 00:15:07,065
I saw that you like sweets.
So I bought you some desserts.

179
00:15:07,865 --> 00:15:09,585
I'm really sorry, Putter.

180
00:15:09,665 --> 00:15:12,105
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry. I really am.

181
00:15:12,185 --> 00:15:13,745
I really didn't know.

182
00:15:14,425 --> 00:15:16,585
You weren't the one
who leaked the clip, right?

183
00:15:16,665 --> 00:15:18,825
No. I wasn't the one who leaked it.

184
00:15:18,905 --> 00:15:20,385
Tell him that.

185
00:15:20,465 --> 00:15:23,665
Well, if you apologize like that…
anyone would think you leaked it.

186
00:15:24,865 --> 00:15:26,425
I'm really sorry. I really am.

187
00:15:27,025 --> 00:15:29,345
I just feel so guilty.

188
00:15:29,425 --> 00:15:31,225
Normally, I'm all for shipping moments,

189
00:15:31,305 --> 00:15:33,985
and when they're real, it's even better.

190
00:15:34,065 --> 00:15:35,625
-Honestly…
-That's enough, Min.

191
00:15:35,705 --> 00:15:37,025
You're making it worse.

192
00:15:38,865 --> 00:15:40,265
I'm sorry.

193
00:15:40,785 --> 00:15:44,265
But when it happened to you…
my best friend,

194
00:15:44,345 --> 00:15:46,185
I felt even worse

195
00:15:46,265 --> 00:15:48,465
for enjoying something
you wanted to keep private.

196
00:15:49,945 --> 00:15:51,065
I'm sorry.

197
00:15:51,945 --> 00:15:54,345
Thank you so much, Min,
for caring about me this much.

198
00:15:55,065 --> 00:15:57,505
I was a little upset,
when people dug this up.

199
00:15:59,465 --> 00:16:01,185
But… I'm over it.

200
00:16:05,585 --> 00:16:06,705
-Really?
-Really.

201
00:16:08,105 --> 00:16:12,345
So… stop feeling guilty. I forgive you.

202
00:16:15,105 --> 00:16:17,585
Nobody's fighting anymore.

203
00:16:17,665 --> 00:16:18,785
LeeIth and I…

204
00:16:21,945 --> 00:16:22,785
are good again.

205
00:16:24,425 --> 00:16:27,585
Come on. You just apologized to him.

206
00:16:30,465 --> 00:16:34,065
I mean… LeeIth and I… are friends again.

207
00:16:51,425 --> 00:16:52,745
Cheers.

208
00:16:56,065 --> 00:16:57,705
-Hey!
-Hey.

209
00:16:57,785 --> 00:16:58,825
-Hey!
-Hello.

210
00:16:58,905 --> 00:17:01,105
-Sit here.
-You bought so many desserts.

211
00:17:01,185 --> 00:17:02,025
Here you go.

212
00:17:02,105 --> 00:17:03,745
-Where's mine?
-Here.

213
00:17:03,825 --> 00:17:05,385
Come sit down. Sit.

214
00:17:05,464 --> 00:17:06,865
Hurry, sit.

215
00:17:06,944 --> 00:17:08,545
-Yeah, I'm coming.
-Wait for me.

216
00:17:09,745 --> 00:17:11,224
I'll put the cups here.

217
00:17:11,305 --> 00:17:12,545
-Go ahead, sit.
-Okay.

218
00:17:13,424 --> 00:17:15,625
-Have a seat.
-Everyone.

219
00:17:15,704 --> 00:17:18,345
Finally, we saved our friendship.

220
00:17:20,184 --> 00:17:22,145
We did it!

221
00:17:22,224 --> 00:17:23,905
Oh, come on.

222
00:17:23,985 --> 00:17:25,464
-Keep it up.
-You're way too excited.

223
00:17:25,545 --> 00:17:26,865
Including me?

224
00:17:26,944 --> 00:17:28,945
Of course. Today wouldn't be
complete without you.

225
00:17:29,025 --> 00:17:31,145
Hey, everyone, look!

226
00:17:31,225 --> 00:17:33,265
Leo's sitting with everyone today.

227
00:17:34,705 --> 00:17:36,265
Scoot over. Hurry.

228
00:17:36,345 --> 00:17:38,905
We're friends now.

229
00:17:38,985 --> 00:17:40,185
Well…

230
00:17:40,825 --> 00:17:43,385
-Okay, okay.
-I'm still excited.

231
00:17:43,465 --> 00:17:46,065
Just to be safe, I'll sit over there.

232
00:17:47,545 --> 00:17:49,265
-Ditching me?
-You seem relaxed today.

233
00:17:49,345 --> 00:17:52,745
Nothing but good news today.
What? What else?

234
00:17:52,825 --> 00:17:54,105
Hit me with all of it!

235
00:17:54,185 --> 00:17:55,385
There is!

236
00:17:55,465 --> 00:17:59,105
We, Lazy Meow Meow…
are playing our first competition at Siam!

237
00:18:01,945 --> 00:18:04,025
Lazy Meow Meow!

238
00:18:04,625 --> 00:18:06,945
-Come on, scream!
-Keep going! Don't interrupt. What else?

239
00:18:07,025 --> 00:18:09,225
-Me! Me!
-Go ahead!

240
00:18:09,305 --> 00:18:11,705
This better be huge, asshole.

241
00:18:11,785 --> 00:18:15,145
It is. Faye and I are officially together!

242
00:18:16,545 --> 00:18:18,145
I knew it!

243
00:18:18,225 --> 00:18:20,465
-In! Faye! In! Faye!
-Indy actually did it!

244
00:18:20,545 --> 00:18:21,945
Didn't you say Faye
always left you on read?

245
00:18:22,025 --> 00:18:23,385
I could handle that.

246
00:18:23,465 --> 00:18:25,145
When did you two start dating?

247
00:18:25,225 --> 00:18:27,065
Yeah, and how did it even happen?

248
00:18:28,905 --> 00:18:30,905
Because of the love note.

249
00:18:33,345 --> 00:18:35,945
I'm so sick,
and I'm sick of this. Allergies.

250
00:18:37,545 --> 00:18:39,145
Get well soon.

251
00:18:42,225 --> 00:18:43,865
Thank you, Indy.

252
00:18:43,945 --> 00:18:45,825
That's where our story began.

253
00:18:45,905 --> 00:18:46,745
1/2 FOOD

254
00:18:51,665 --> 00:18:53,505
Make sure to eat… and take your medicine.

255
00:18:55,585 --> 00:18:58,665
I brought meals…
and medicine to Faye all week long.

256
00:19:05,625 --> 00:19:06,585
Indy.

257
00:19:09,425 --> 00:19:10,585
Faye.

258
00:19:20,545 --> 00:19:22,305
Thank you, Indy.

259
00:19:22,385 --> 00:19:24,025
The medicine worked wonders.

260
00:19:25,425 --> 00:19:27,145
You're welcome.

261
00:19:27,225 --> 00:19:30,185
Then I'll… get going.

262
00:19:39,785 --> 00:19:40,785
Wait.

263
00:19:41,705 --> 00:19:44,905
-Can I ask you something?
-Sure.

264
00:19:46,945 --> 00:19:51,305
From now on…
would you bring me meals every day?

265
00:20:02,065 --> 00:20:02,985
You mean…

266
00:20:14,425 --> 00:20:17,785
Woo-hoo!

267
00:20:18,465 --> 00:20:20,265
My friend's got a girlfriend!

268
00:20:20,345 --> 00:20:21,905
Put your head on her shoulder!

269
00:20:21,985 --> 00:20:23,785
How are you this smooth?

270
00:20:25,145 --> 00:20:26,385
Something like that.

271
00:20:26,465 --> 00:20:29,905
Proud of me, Doc? Making my own decisions?

272
00:20:31,665 --> 00:20:33,105
How's it going with Faye?

273
00:20:33,185 --> 00:20:35,345
Let me know when you two get married.

274
00:20:37,065 --> 00:20:40,865
-Indy! Indy!
-Cut it out, asshole.

275
00:20:40,945 --> 00:20:43,145
I'll keep you updated.

276
00:20:46,945 --> 00:20:48,705
I'm already getting ready for the wedding.

277
00:20:48,785 --> 00:20:50,945
Did you see what I sent you?

278
00:20:51,025 --> 00:20:52,665
Which outfit should I wear?

279
00:20:52,745 --> 00:20:54,665
You said you didn't need
my help deciding anymore.

280
00:20:55,905 --> 00:20:57,185
Are you sulking?

281
00:20:57,705 --> 00:20:58,825
No.

282
00:20:58,905 --> 00:21:00,705
It's just that some dog asked,

283
00:21:00,785 --> 00:21:03,585
"Are you proud of me
for making my own decisions?"

284
00:21:05,305 --> 00:21:08,185
Well, Faye's really serious
about dressing up.

285
00:21:08,705 --> 00:21:10,185
I'm only asking you to pick an outfit.

286
00:21:10,265 --> 00:21:12,265
Not to choose my path in life.

287
00:21:13,425 --> 00:21:15,465
You're still asking me to decide for you.

288
00:21:16,025 --> 00:21:18,825
Fine. I'll choose it myself.

289
00:21:18,905 --> 00:21:21,825
Think Faye and I will work out?

290
00:21:22,345 --> 00:21:24,945
Why ask me? What's making you hesitate?

291
00:21:25,025 --> 00:21:28,185
Don't know. I just feel… weird.

292
00:21:28,265 --> 00:21:32,065
Like… my heart's not beating normally.

293
00:21:33,505 --> 00:21:35,145
Maybe you should see a doctor.

294
00:21:35,905 --> 00:21:38,345
I am. Fortune Teller Jia's right here.

295
00:21:38,425 --> 00:21:39,705
Draw me a card.

296
00:21:48,985 --> 00:21:50,825
One question, then let me sleep.

297
00:22:01,425 --> 00:22:04,825
Calm down… and think of that person.
The one you like.

298
00:22:06,225 --> 00:22:08,145
The one you feel at ease with.

299
00:22:28,585 --> 00:22:30,225
Your mind's not settled. I can't read it.

300
00:22:33,985 --> 00:22:36,065
How… did you know?

301
00:22:36,145 --> 00:22:37,385
You're shaking even more now.

302
00:22:39,385 --> 00:22:42,225
Then never mind. Good night.

303
00:23:00,785 --> 00:23:02,385
Will this one do?

304
00:23:06,345 --> 00:23:07,745
It's pretty good.

305
00:23:07,825 --> 00:23:10,985
Or if you don't like it,
I can take another one.

306
00:23:11,065 --> 00:23:14,225
It's okay. Let me take some
of you instead.

307
00:23:17,065 --> 00:23:18,025
Here we go.

308
00:23:18,865 --> 00:23:20,745
One… two…

309
00:23:20,825 --> 00:23:22,865
Move a little to the left.

310
00:23:22,945 --> 00:23:24,785
Lean forward a little.

311
00:23:24,865 --> 00:23:25,745
Okay.

312
00:23:28,145 --> 00:23:29,225
That's a shame.

313
00:23:29,305 --> 00:23:31,425
Your outfit doesn't really match
the café today.

314
00:23:35,585 --> 00:23:36,705
Really?

315
00:23:37,705 --> 00:23:39,545
I thought you'd coordinate your outfit.

316
00:23:41,385 --> 00:23:42,305
That's news to me.

317
00:23:42,905 --> 00:23:44,825
Didn't know I had to match my outfit too.

318
00:23:44,905 --> 00:23:47,425
Let's try again next time.
You'll get better photos.

319
00:23:48,865 --> 00:23:49,785
Let's eat.

320
00:24:01,425 --> 00:24:04,385
-You seem a little nervous.
-Do I?

321
00:24:04,465 --> 00:24:06,145
FORTUNE TELLER JIA

322
00:24:11,425 --> 00:24:12,345
Hello?

323
00:24:13,745 --> 00:24:14,705
Where are you?

324
00:24:15,905 --> 00:24:17,025
You okay?

325
00:24:18,425 --> 00:24:20,025
We can talk when you're free.

326
00:24:20,665 --> 00:24:21,905
I'm still okay.

327
00:24:36,585 --> 00:24:38,545
I'm in the middle of the bridge.

328
00:24:38,625 --> 00:24:40,105
Me too.

329
00:24:40,185 --> 00:24:44,345
There's lotus flowers…
banana trees… and a waterfall.

330
00:24:44,425 --> 00:24:45,465
And trees.

331
00:24:46,625 --> 00:24:48,065
-I see you.
-Have you found me yet?

332
00:25:01,185 --> 00:25:03,025
Hop on.

333
00:25:06,025 --> 00:25:08,145
I'll pedal. You just sit there.

334
00:25:10,745 --> 00:25:11,865
Let's go.

335
00:25:15,625 --> 00:25:16,905
Careful. Pedestrians.

336
00:25:43,745 --> 00:25:45,145
So? Having fun?

337
00:25:45,225 --> 00:25:47,305
Yeah… but I'm exhausted.

338
00:25:55,985 --> 00:25:57,145
You okay?

339
00:25:58,825 --> 00:25:59,985
I'm fine.

340
00:26:01,505 --> 00:26:03,625
Remember… what I told you?

341
00:26:03,705 --> 00:26:05,785
What the cards say isn't always true.

342
00:26:06,785 --> 00:26:07,625
Yeah.

343
00:26:10,225 --> 00:26:12,945
The cards once showed
my parents would fall in love again.

344
00:26:14,905 --> 00:26:16,185
But they didn't.

345
00:26:46,145 --> 00:26:48,025
You can let your guard down with me.

346
00:26:52,865 --> 00:26:57,465
Breathe in. Breathe out.

347
00:26:57,545 --> 00:27:01,065
Let everything bottled up inside out.

348
00:27:04,865 --> 00:27:06,505
You're making fun of my mom, asshole.

349
00:27:08,625 --> 00:27:10,025
But I tried it, and it really works.

350
00:27:10,625 --> 00:27:12,105
That's because you did it in a room.

351
00:27:12,185 --> 00:27:15,225
Standing there… throwing leaves at me.
Nothing to be embarrassed about.

352
00:27:16,425 --> 00:27:18,425
Come on, I'll do it with you.

353
00:27:23,105 --> 00:27:25,585
Come on. Together.

354
00:27:26,425 --> 00:27:27,825
One…

355
00:27:27,905 --> 00:27:29,265
Two…

356
00:27:29,345 --> 00:27:30,305
Three…

357
00:27:30,385 --> 00:27:32,105
Breathe in.

358
00:27:32,945 --> 00:27:34,065
Breathe out.

359
00:27:36,105 --> 00:27:37,585
Breathe in.

360
00:27:38,585 --> 00:27:39,985
Breathe out.

361
00:27:44,345 --> 00:27:46,505
Let those feelings out. Breathe out.

362
00:27:51,625 --> 00:27:54,105
Come on, one last time.

363
00:27:54,185 --> 00:27:55,665
Breathe in.

364
00:27:55,745 --> 00:27:58,105
Let those bottled-up feelings out.

365
00:28:18,665 --> 00:28:20,545
So? Feeling better?

366
00:28:20,625 --> 00:28:22,465
Even more extreme than what my mom does.

367
00:28:23,465 --> 00:28:24,785
But it does feel liberating.

368
00:28:26,425 --> 00:28:27,385
Thanks.

369
00:28:35,225 --> 00:28:37,505
And you being here with me…

370
00:28:37,585 --> 00:28:39,105
Won't Faye mind?

371
00:28:41,225 --> 00:28:42,145
Well…

372
00:28:43,185 --> 00:28:44,145
She won't.

373
00:28:46,225 --> 00:28:48,985
Faye. I'll get going now.

374
00:28:49,065 --> 00:28:50,785
I have something urgent to take care of.

375
00:29:00,865 --> 00:29:03,305
Let's go get some snacks.
Let's get some sugar.

376
00:29:03,385 --> 00:29:04,585
Sure.

377
00:29:13,265 --> 00:29:14,185
Your bag.

378
00:29:26,065 --> 00:29:28,745
-School's over. Want to go to Siam?
-Nah.

379
00:29:28,825 --> 00:29:30,625
Today's our anniversary.

380
00:29:30,705 --> 00:29:32,825
-We're going to celebrate.
-LeeIth.

381
00:29:34,665 --> 00:29:36,345
I came over to say hi, LeeIth.

382
00:29:36,425 --> 00:29:38,025
You can just call me "Lee."

383
00:29:39,105 --> 00:29:40,105
Okay.

384
00:29:40,185 --> 00:29:42,745
This is actually my first time
meeting you in person.

385
00:29:42,825 --> 00:29:45,105
Same here. Nice to meet you.

386
00:29:46,105 --> 00:29:48,945
Then I'll text you later.

387
00:29:49,025 --> 00:29:50,665
Okay. Bye-bye.

388
00:29:55,945 --> 00:29:56,865
Your friend?

389
00:29:57,665 --> 00:30:01,065
Yeah. Lately, she's been
trying to hit on me.

390
00:30:02,305 --> 00:30:03,145
She's hitting on him.

391
00:30:03,225 --> 00:30:06,905
You know, I think…
this one doesn't seem closeted.

392
00:30:07,785 --> 00:30:09,745
I've been pretty open lately.

393
00:30:10,345 --> 00:30:12,825
Open-minded. Yeah.

394
00:30:12,905 --> 00:30:15,585
After tutoring, want to head back with me?

395
00:30:16,145 --> 00:30:19,185
I… was planning to watch
a movie at Paragon.

396
00:30:20,865 --> 00:30:21,705
Sure.

397
00:30:34,985 --> 00:30:35,905
Here you go.

398
00:30:44,505 --> 00:30:45,705
Here, this is for you.

399
00:30:51,745 --> 00:30:54,265
Who's cheering for me? Let me hear you!

400
00:30:55,785 --> 00:30:56,945
Thank you…

401
00:31:03,505 --> 00:31:04,385
Want some?

402
00:31:07,825 --> 00:31:08,745
No, thanks.

403
00:31:15,625 --> 00:31:17,345
Fantastic Four is out now.

404
00:31:19,265 --> 00:31:20,985
Yeah. Have you seen it yet?

405
00:31:21,585 --> 00:31:24,065
Not yet. I was planning to watch it today.

406
00:31:24,145 --> 00:31:27,385
I heard the new phase is pretty exciting.

407
00:31:28,105 --> 00:31:29,345
Want to go watch it?

408
00:31:30,625 --> 00:31:32,985
It's okay. I've changed my mind.

409
00:31:33,065 --> 00:31:35,265
I'd rather not watch it.
Come on, let's go upstairs.

410
00:31:53,265 --> 00:31:55,185
-Hey.
-Putter.

411
00:31:56,625 --> 00:31:58,225
-Here, eat.
-Hey, hey, hey!

412
00:31:58,305 --> 00:31:59,865
-Go ahead, eat.
-Have some of my drink.

413
00:31:59,945 --> 00:32:02,145
-Go on, eat.
-Want some snacks?

414
00:32:02,225 --> 00:32:03,545
That's enough.

415
00:32:03,625 --> 00:32:04,905
This is getting a little too sweet.

416
00:32:04,985 --> 00:32:07,585
Come on. We don't want
our friend to feel lonely.

417
00:32:07,665 --> 00:32:10,105
Look, Proud even postponed
where we're going to celebrate

418
00:32:10,185 --> 00:32:11,585
just so she could see you off.

419
00:32:13,385 --> 00:32:15,825
We're Putter's bodyguard squad.

420
00:32:15,905 --> 00:32:17,825
Oh, you're so cringe.

421
00:32:17,905 --> 00:32:19,985
So, are you into bodyguard plots?

422
00:32:20,065 --> 00:32:22,745
Obviously! I love them!

423
00:32:24,945 --> 00:32:27,985
The store where I'm a member
is offering 50% off.

424
00:32:28,065 --> 00:32:28,945
Let's go buy something.

425
00:32:29,545 --> 00:32:30,865
-Hurry up!
-That sounds good!

426
00:32:30,945 --> 00:32:32,625
You keep sulking. I'll be right back.

427
00:32:32,705 --> 00:32:35,105
-Go!
-Hurry up!

428
00:32:35,705 --> 00:32:36,985
One day, it'll get better.

429
00:32:37,065 --> 00:32:39,465
If you want to be sad, then be sad.

430
00:32:39,545 --> 00:32:41,665
You can move on whenever you're ready.

431
00:32:41,745 --> 00:32:43,305
People can't control their feelings.

432
00:32:43,385 --> 00:32:44,825
That's advice from an emotional girl.

433
00:32:46,705 --> 00:32:49,465
Okay. Then you'll be
seeing me sad for a while.

434
00:32:49,545 --> 00:32:51,265
I'm ready.

435
00:32:55,425 --> 00:32:56,945
Hey, you guys go on ahead.

436
00:32:57,025 --> 00:32:58,225
Go, go, go!

437
00:33:14,385 --> 00:33:19,985
NEED ADVICE? ASK LEE

438
00:33:20,065 --> 00:33:23,025
This chat's been dead for ages.
Why did you come in here?

439
00:33:23,665 --> 00:33:25,865
I need your advice about something.

440
00:33:26,745 --> 00:33:28,865
It's about Faye.

441
00:33:30,385 --> 00:33:32,865
Faye's been acting
kind of weird around me.

442
00:33:32,945 --> 00:33:35,225
Everyone keeps messaging me,
asking what I did.

443
00:33:35,305 --> 00:33:37,025
They all say I look better now.

444
00:33:37,105 --> 00:33:41,185
I want to buy more clothes.
Can you take me to Siam again?

445
00:33:41,265 --> 00:33:42,425
FAYE

446
00:33:42,505 --> 00:33:44,505
-And then I… I mean, she…
-She didn't tell you

447
00:33:44,585 --> 00:33:47,425
-thinks Jia and I are really close.
-to tell someone else about it.

448
00:33:49,825 --> 00:33:50,905
She didn't say anything.

449
00:33:50,985 --> 00:33:54,105
She just keeps asking me about Jia.

450
00:33:54,185 --> 00:33:55,625
Here's the thing, though.

451
00:33:56,705 --> 00:33:58,665
I just feel guilty that I…

452
00:33:59,265 --> 00:34:02,585
that I feel more comfortable
being with Jia than Faye.

453
00:34:02,665 --> 00:34:05,225
I feel like talking to him more than Faye.

454
00:34:06,825 --> 00:34:08,344
Do you want my opinion?

455
00:34:08,425 --> 00:34:11,225
Of course I do.
If I didn't, I wouldn't be here.

456
00:34:12,744 --> 00:34:14,824
As your Best Friend of the Year
for seven years…

457
00:34:16,264 --> 00:34:17,304
Making fun of me?

458
00:34:17,865 --> 00:34:22,264
I think… you're starting to fall for Jia.
You're totally hooked on him.

459
00:34:24,385 --> 00:34:28,665
Honestly, I feel that way too,
but… I just needed someone to confirm it.

460
00:34:32,665 --> 00:34:33,625
But…

461
00:34:35,105 --> 00:34:36,425
I think

462
00:34:38,185 --> 00:34:40,425
dating someone close to you
never works out.

463
00:34:42,225 --> 00:34:44,145
There'll probably be problems someday.

464
00:34:45,545 --> 00:34:47,425
But the biggest shame is…

465
00:34:48,945 --> 00:34:50,505
losing the friendship.

466
00:34:55,225 --> 00:34:56,824
That's why I came to you.

467
00:34:58,225 --> 00:35:01,025
So… who did you go see a movie with?

468
00:35:01,105 --> 00:35:03,105
I was trying to keep
an open mind and move on.

469
00:35:04,625 --> 00:35:06,265
But I'm still going in circles.

470
00:35:09,185 --> 00:35:10,385
Lee, I…

471
00:35:12,145 --> 00:35:13,985
-Huh?
-Hey, Lee.

472
00:35:14,065 --> 00:35:16,385
I made shrimp rice porridge. Want some?

473
00:35:16,465 --> 00:35:18,145
Sure. Thank you.

474
00:35:20,185 --> 00:35:22,225
-Want some?
-Yeah. Bring it over.

475
00:35:41,105 --> 00:35:42,785
Then how about we go see Fantastic Four?

476
00:35:47,585 --> 00:35:50,945
Someone asked me
to see a movie that day, but I…

477
00:35:51,545 --> 00:35:53,665
Sorry, I have something urgent today.

478
00:35:53,745 --> 00:35:55,225
Let's do it another time.

479
00:35:58,785 --> 00:36:01,105
That's too bad, but it's okay.

480
00:36:01,705 --> 00:36:03,425
I just got to Paragon.

481
00:36:09,025 --> 00:36:10,865
If you really want to move on,

482
00:36:10,945 --> 00:36:14,465
Jia once told me to try something new.

483
00:36:14,545 --> 00:36:17,105
Yeah. I did.

484
00:36:17,945 --> 00:36:20,785
You have to be serious about it.
Like I was.

485
00:36:20,865 --> 00:36:25,585
Back then, I… bought new clothes,
found new things to do,

486
00:36:25,665 --> 00:36:27,265
and deleted all of Faye's contacts.

487
00:36:28,065 --> 00:36:29,825
Then how did you get back together?

488
00:36:30,505 --> 00:36:32,625
I thought I'd already moved on.

489
00:36:32,705 --> 00:36:34,945
So I followed her on Instagram again.

490
00:36:35,025 --> 00:36:37,665
-So, did you actually move on?
-Good question.

491
00:36:37,745 --> 00:36:39,185
Does that even count as moving on?

492
00:36:39,265 --> 00:36:40,465
What's wrong with us?

493
00:37:19,025 --> 00:37:22,265
Damn. Chicken rice, thigh meat, no skin.

494
00:37:23,345 --> 00:37:26,145
Yeah. I finished making it,
then remembered you like it.

495
00:37:51,745 --> 00:37:52,705
How is it?

496
00:37:54,385 --> 00:37:55,425
It's pretty good.

497
00:37:56,865 --> 00:37:57,865
And it was free.

498
00:37:58,665 --> 00:38:00,025
I won't starve this month.

499
00:38:01,225 --> 00:38:02,825
Yeah, eat up.

500
00:38:27,985 --> 00:38:29,265
Don't rush. You'll choke.

501
00:38:29,345 --> 00:38:31,025
I'm running late. I have band practice.

502
00:38:32,305 --> 00:38:34,985
No, no, no. I'll clean up.

503
00:38:36,265 --> 00:38:37,345
You're the best, Buddy.

504
00:39:05,265 --> 00:39:08,665
Trying to make conversation
with you here is kind of exhausting.

505
00:39:22,385 --> 00:39:26,705
THANKS. I'M READY FOR TOMORROW.

506
00:39:26,785 --> 00:39:32,865
LAZY MEOW MEOW - WE'RE READY
PLEASE COME SEE US, EVERYONE.

507
00:39:39,505 --> 00:39:42,065
"Lazy Meow Meow." What the heck is that?

508
00:39:43,825 --> 00:39:47,345
-It's our band's name.
-Seriously?

509
00:39:47,985 --> 00:39:49,985
I've wondered about that too.

510
00:39:50,065 --> 00:39:51,825
The band's name is one thing,

511
00:39:51,905 --> 00:39:54,905
but I'm more curious
why you made a logo for the band.

512
00:39:55,745 --> 00:39:59,145
Well, didn't you tell me
to do what I like?

513
00:40:00,065 --> 00:40:02,105
I thought it'd be something about gaming.

514
00:40:03,265 --> 00:40:04,305
I'd better get going.

515
00:40:17,505 --> 00:40:19,185
COMPETITION DAY

516
00:40:19,265 --> 00:40:21,865
Hello, everyone.

517
00:40:22,545 --> 00:40:28,585
Welcome, to the New Wave Band Contest.

518
00:40:29,865 --> 00:40:31,545
Move over. I'm here.

519
00:40:31,625 --> 00:40:32,785
Hey, Bro.

520
00:40:32,865 --> 00:40:35,345
-Did you run all the way here?
-I parked over there.

521
00:40:35,425 --> 00:40:37,145
-You came straight here?
-Yeah.

522
00:40:37,225 --> 00:40:38,865
Good. You're here.

523
00:40:38,945 --> 00:40:40,465
-Hi!
-Hi!

524
00:40:40,545 --> 00:40:42,945
-Hey, Fang's here too?
-They'll be here any second.

525
00:40:43,025 --> 00:40:44,105
Don't turn around yet.

526
00:40:56,905 --> 00:40:58,145
Where's Lee?

527
00:41:01,585 --> 00:41:03,745
Lee!

